-10-30T13:14:28Z"},{"number":405,"title":"Integrate with https://pre-commit.com/ ","comments":42,"created_at":"2022-06-30T04:29:24Z"},{"number":4745,"title":"CLI --help font or character format trouble when PAGER=less and LESS is unset (Alpine/Gentoo/NixOS default)","comments":39,"created_at":"2024-10-31T22:42:50Z"}],"discussions":[{"number":10685,"title":"Colocation without Automatic Export","comments":1,"category":"Q&A","created_at":"2026-11-13T13:46:52Z"},{"number":10653,"title":"Does jj allow for simultaneously applied virtual branches like GitButler?","comments":1,"category":"Q&A","created_at":"2026-11-08T17:10:25Z"},{"number":10597,"title":"v0.47.1","comments":0,"category":"General","created_at":"2026-11-05T00:34:13Z"},{"number":10586,"title":"v0.47.0","comments":1,"category":"General","created_at":"2026-11-04T17:52:42Z"},{"number":10504,"title":"Proposal: a `followlines(file, lines)` revset function, like Mercurial's","comments":3,"category":"Ideas","created_at":"2026-10-27T01:46:13Z"},{"number":10442,"title":"Using jj workspaces for parallel coding agents","comments":1,"category":"Show and tell","created_at":"2026-10-22T09:22:26Z"},{"number":10431,"title":"How do I add another parent to a Jujutsu commit?","comments":2,"category":"Q&A","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:40:47Z"},{"number":10429,"title":"jj-watch, simple bash script to get real time tree and status preview","comments":1,"category":"General","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:12:20Z"}],"latest_release":{"name":"v0.47.1","tag":"v0.47.1","published_at":"2026-11-05T00:34:13Z","body":"This release fixes a dependency error that broke Linux builds in the 0.47.0\r\nrelease.\r\n\r\n### About\r\n\r\njj is a Git-compatible version control system that is both simple and powerful.\r\nSee the [installation instructions](https://docs.jj-vcs.dev/v0.47.1/install-and-setup/) to get started.\r\n\r\n### Deprecations\r\n\r\n* The `git.sign-on-push` boolean option is deprecated in favor of the\r\n  `revsets.git-sign-on-push` revset. The default value is `none()`. If\r\n  `git.sign-on-push` was previously set to `true`, it will be migrated to\r\n  `revsets.git-sign-on-push = \"~signed() & mine()\"`.\r\n\r\n### New features\r\n\r\n* New `revsets.git-sign-on-push` config option containing the revset of\r\n  commits to be signed when `jj git push` is run. It replaces the\r\n  `git.sign-on-push` boolean option.\r\n\r\n### Contributors\r\n\r\nThanks to the people who made this release happen!\r\n\r\n* Philippe Daouadi (@blastrock)\r\n","is_prerelease":false},"readme":true,"readme_zh":false,"news":[],"stale":false,"snapshot_at":"2026-11-14T08:50:43Z","history_start":"2026-09-06"}